                <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
                    <div class="col-md-6 col-12">
                        <img src="~/Content/img/Course/ce.png" class="rounded-4 dept-img" style="width: 98%; height:250px;" alt="Civil Engineering" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-6 col-12 mt-4 mt-md-0">
                        <h2 style="font-weight: 600; color: #0747ae;">CIVIL ENGINEERING</h2>
                        <hr style="border:1px solid black;" />
                        <p style="font-size: 18px; color: black; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify;">
                            B.Tech. program in Civil Engineering offers a comprehensive education in the planning, design, construction, and maintenance of infrastructure essential to modern society. The core curriculum covers key areas such as Structural Engineering, Geotechnical Engineering, Transportation Engineering, Water Resources Engineering, Environmental Engineering, and Construction Technology and Management. 
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="row mt-4">
                    <div class="col-12">
                        <p style="font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.8; color: black; text-align: justify;">
                            Students gain both theoretical understanding and hands-on experience through laboratory work, design projects, and field training. With the growing need for smart, sustainable, and resilient infrastructure, the program integrates emerging topics like Sustainable Construction Practices, Environmental Impact Assessment, Smart City Planning, Intelligent Transportation Systems (ITS), and Climate-Responsive Infrastructure. Students are also introduced to advanced tools and technologies such as Building Information Modeling (BIM), Geographic Information Systems (GIS), Remote Sensing, and Construction Automation. This blend of traditional knowledge and modern innovation equips graduates to address global challenges in urbanization, climate change, and resource management, preparing them for impactful careers in public infrastructure, urban development, consultancy, and research.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
               


